dd a note and the call carries on with other products. Hardship offers a transfer to `mtb_care`, and if the customer declines it adds a note. A second refusal to talk ends the call.

Some P12 rules have no field in the schema, so the audit lists them as unresolved and they'll need to go into the prompt text. They include:
- don't give account details to relatives;
- strip spaces from text answers;
- make one counteroffer at the floor when the customer offers less;
- never offer discounts or instalment plans;
- a correction cancels the customer's consent;
- never say a failed promise was saved.
